il exports rise"}],"revisions":[],"entities":[{"name":"Iran","kind":"place","mentions":11},{"name":"Hormuz","kind":"person","mentions":6},{"name":"Strait of Hormuz","kind":"place","mentions":5},{"name":"India","kind":"place","mentions":4},{"name":"Indian","kind":"group","mentions":4},{"name":"Qatar","kind":"place","mentions":4},{"name":"China","kind":"place","mentions":3},{"name":"Iraq","kind":"place","mentions":3},{"name":"Strait","kind":"place","mentions":2},{"name":"Iranian Government","kind":"organisation","mentions":1}],"disputes":[],"summary":{"text":"Iran has exempted Indian ships from transit restrictions in the Strait of Hormuz. This is the first time Iran has exempted ships from India, China, Iraq, and Qatar from Hormuz transit restrictions. The move is part of Iran's efforts to ease tensions with India and improve relations between the two countries. The Strait of Hormuz is a waterway between the Persian Gulf and the Gulf of Oman. On the north coast lies Iran, and on the south coast lies the Musandam Peninsula under the Musandam Governorate of Oman, with a portion of the southwest of the peninsula under the United Arab Emirates (UAE). The strait is about 104 miles long, with a width varying from about 60 mi to 24 mi.","text_hi":null,"model":"qwen2.5-1.5b-instruct-q4_k_m.gguf","created_at":"2026-11-04T21:25:45Z"},"context":{"background":[{"title":"Strait of Hormuz","extract":"The Strait of Hormuz is a waterway between the Persian Gulf and the Gulf of Oman. On the north coast lies Iran, and on the south coast lies the Musandam Peninsula under the Musandam Governorate of Oman, with a portion of the southwest of the peninsula under the United Arab Emirates (UAE). The strait is about 104 miles long, with a width varying from about 60 mi to 24 mi.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strait_of_Hormuz","source":"Wikipedia","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"places":[{"title":"Iran","extract":"Iran, officially the Islamic Republic of Iran, and historically known as Persia, is a country in West Asia. It borders Iraq to the west; Turkey, Azerbaijan, and Armenia to the northwest; the Caspian Sea to the north, Turkmenistan to the northeast; Afghanistan to the east; Pakistan to the southeast; and the Gulf of Oman and the Persian Gulf to the south. With a population of over 92 million, Iran ranks 17th globally in both geographic size and population. It is divided into five regions with 31 provinces. Tehran is the nation's capital and largest city and serves as its primary economic center.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iran","source":"Wikipedia","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","iso2":"IR"},{"title":"India","extract":"India, officially the Republic of India, is a country in South Asia. It is the world's seventh-largest country by area and its most populous. Bounded by the Indian Ocean on the south, the Arabian Sea on the southwest, and the Bay of Bengal on the southeast, it shares land borders with Pakistan to the west, China, Nepal, and Bhutan to the north, and Bangladesh and Myanmar to the east. In the Indian Ocean, India is near Sri Lanka and the Maldives.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/India","source":"Wikipedia","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","iso2":"IN"}],"arc":{"reports":239,"first_seen":"2026-10-09T18:01:09Z","first_title":"Tanker attacks in Strait of Hormuz surge to wartime high as Iran tries to choke off oil exports","first_url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMigwFBVV95cUxQLXQ5SXNEMzB0UFVEM09pZjB6S29PbXBPZWdwQ1VUei1iSkJ4RWx6d0pvOUhRVXdiVTZKeHUzUkVVSUE5bmtENm5OOXFrN24zYjhYdlN5R1VfckRfaGt3eXJlLXVNSFR6OE5lTTdWT19mRGVRNDQ5QTltV09OdXdSd2h6cw?oc=5","first_publisher":"CNBC","earlier":[{"id":"e_4cd562e5d20e","title":"Is the Strait of Hormuz Really Safe After the Iran War?","date":"2026-11-06T05:00:57Z","url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMimAFBVV95cUxQU0JHTjhaenZJV0dHMmNCQTNydDVHZWNoYS1yREl5dWFVWWUtUHFuZ1dNby1YUVlPMFBlRjdsMWZNTkdBWUZpVFQ1a1dsQ3dRc3BvcWs4LUl2allneFhWMGExcHQyeWhlUGFPWk5tMlNzel9xTF9uUnRYUHhWMWZnM3d5en